libsurface (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * surface_colour no longer copies from a NULL list of length 0.
  * The fuzz harnesses follow the OSS Verify build contract; the key a
    backend receives for an LED is a checked property of the board harness.
  * No change to the library ABI.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

libsurface (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The DigiNet module's tests build against libdiginet-emu, the desk
    emulator and child harness libdiginet 0.1.8 installs, and this tree's
    copies are gone; a check keeps them from coming back, and reads at least
    one file (#18).
  * Every dependency on libdiginet and libmackie states a floor and a ceiling
    (libdiginet >= 0.1.4, build >= 0.1.8, and << 0.2; libmackie >= 0.1.0 and
    << 0.2).
  * The commit-message and private-reference checks are the shared ones; the
    local copy is gone.
  * The packages install their licence and a short README and no other
    markdown; their descriptions point to openmixer.org.
  * No change to the library or its ABI.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

